#part("Part 1: Trigonometric and hyperbolic identities")

#topic("Trigonometric identities")

#ident("I1", [$ sin^2 alpha + cos^2 alpha = 1 $], [Pythagorean identity; recovers either function from the other])
#ident("I2", [$ cos 2 alpha = cos^2 alpha - sin^2 alpha = 2 cos^2 alpha - 1 = 1 - 2 sin^2 alpha $], [double angle for cosine; rewrites cos^2 in integrals, the ground-state ⟨x²⟩ split uses it])
#ident("I3", [$ sin 2 alpha = 2 sin alpha cos alpha $], [double angle for sine])
#ident("I4", [$ sin^2 alpha = (1 - cos 2 alpha)/2 $, $ cos^2 alpha = (1 + cos 2 alpha)/2 $], [half-angle powers; the ground-state ⟨x²⟩ split uses these])
#ident("I5", [$ sin theta = 2 sin(theta/2) cos(theta/2) $], [sine in half angles; the Rutherford dσ/dΩ chain cancels sin theta against two half-angle factors])
#ident("I6", [$ sin(theta/2) = sqrt((1 - cos theta)/2) $], [half-angle radical; inverts cos theta in the Rutherford b(theta) chain])
#ident("I7", [$ cos theta sin theta = 1/2 sin 2 theta $], [product as a single sine; evaluates the cos theta sin theta hemisphere integral])

#topic("Averages and sums")

#ident("I8", [$ ⟨cos^2 theta⟩_"hemisphere" = 1/3 $], [isotropy average; photon-gas radiation pressure p = u/3 and the kinetic-theory pressure])
#ident("I9", [$ integral_0^L sin^2 (n pi x / L) dif x = L/2 $], [box normalisation and every ⟨sin^2⟩ average])
#ident("I10", [$ sum_(n=0)^infinity x^n = 1/(1-x) $, $ sum_(n=0)^infinity n x^n = x/(1-x)^2 $ for $ abs(x) < 1 $], [Planck's mean-energy sum collapses through the geometric series and its derivative])

#topic("Euler's formula")

#ident("I11", [$ e^(i alpha) = cos alpha + i sin alpha $, $ cos alpha = (e^(i alpha) + e^(-i alpha))/2 $, $ sin alpha = (e^(i alpha) - e^(-i alpha))/(2 i) $], [complex exponentials and trig functions carry the same information; box and finite-well solution spaces swap between them])
#ident("I12", [$ e^(plus.minus i k x) = cos k x plus.minus i sin k x $], [the wave-function form used in the box, the finite well, and the parity rewrites])

#topic("Hyperbolic identities")

#ident("I13", [$ sinh x = (e^x - e^(-x))/2 $, $ cosh x = (e^x + e^(-x))/2 $], [hyperbolic form of the barrier interior and free-region solutions])
#ident("I14", [$ cosh^2 x - sinh^2 x = 1 $], [Pythagorean hyperbolic identity])
#ident("I15", [$ e^(kappa L) - e^(-kappa L) = 2 sinh(kappa L) $, $ e^(kappa L) + e^(-kappa L) = 2 cosh(kappa L) $], [the tunnelling T denominator reduces through these])

#topic("Applications of the identities")
#ident("T1", [$⟨ g ⟩ = integral g(v_x) f(v_x) dif v_x$ with $integral f(v_x) dif v_x = 1$], [momentum integral definition])
#ident("T2", [$⟨ v^2 ⟩ = 3 ⟨ v_x^2 ⟩$], [isotropy step of pressure chain])
#ident("T3", [$1/E = lambda /(h c)$], [energy-to-wavelength conversion step])
#ident("T5", [$k = (2 pi)/lambda$], [mode-count change of variable])
#ident("T6", [$integral_0^(2 pi ) dif phi integral_0^( pi/2) cos theta sin theta  dif theta = 2 pi times ((1)/(2)) = pi$], [factor $pi$ in $I_lambda = pi B_lambda$])
#ident("T8", [$f = c/lambda$], [turns $h f$ into $(h c)/lambda$ in every spectrum formula])
#ident("T9", [$E = (h c)/lambda$], [wavelength chain])
#ident("T11", [$E = K + V$ with $V = -e^2/(4 pi epsilon.alt_0 r)$], [planetary-energy and ladder chains])
#ident("T12", [de Broglie $lambda = h/p$], [all three diffraction experiments and the orbit chain])
#ident("T13", [$Delta k dot.c Delta x ≥ 1/2$ with $p = planck k$], [wave-packet bound chain])
#ident("T14", [$p = planck k$ turns $Delta k dot.c Delta x ≥ 1/2$ into $Delta x dot.c Delta p ≥ planck/2$], [localisation bound chain])
#ident("T16", [de Broglie $lambda = h/p$ closes the standing-wave quantisation loop], [standing-wave route])
#ident("T17", [$hat(p) e^(i k x) = -i planck (i k)e^(i k x) = planck k e^(i k x)$], [momentum-representation derivation])
#ident("T18", [$E = p^2/2m + V$ survives as operator identity $hat(H) = hat(K) + hat(V)$], [operator construction])
#ident("T21", [Taylor expansion with $V_1 = 0$ at minimum], [harmonic approximation])

