#step("zero-point minimisation", 2, [$(dif E)/(dif Delta x) = - planck^2/(4m( Delta x)^3) + m omega^2 Delta x = 0$ gives $Delta x^4 = planck^2/(4m^2 omega^2)$, so $Delta x = sqrt( planck /(2m omega ))$])
#step("zero-point minimisation", 3, [at $Delta x^2 = planck /(2m omega )$ the confinement and potential terms each equal $(planck omega)/4$, so the minimum is $E = (planck omega)/2$])
